# Vanity URLs for printed material and campaigns.
#
# Read from the publish directory by both Cloudflare and Netlify.
#
# Each lands on the index page carrying a src tag, so the hero skin and the
# attribution both come from the ONE normal first-touch path — there is no
# second mechanism that could disagree with the sheet. The prefix is what
# selects the segment, per SRC_SEGMENTS in script.js:
#
#   deed- -> movein      dh- -> pro       (no tag) -> direct
#
# 302, not 301: these are marketing URLs and a permanently cached redirect is
# painful to undo once browsers have it.

/movein   /?src=deed-movein   302
/clean    /?src=dh-clean      302

# Business cards.
#
# THESE LIVE HERE, NOT IN THE CLOUDFLARE DASHBOARD. A rule created in the
# dashboard is invisible to this repo and to the test below, which is exactly
# how /q first shipped pointing at an untagged URL. A vanity path in this file
# gets checked; one in the dashboard gets checked by whoever remembers.
#
# The -01 is a PRINT RUN version, not decoration. Reprint with a different
# design and it becomes -02: same channel, two slugs, and the sheet reports
# which card stock or layout actually converted. Free to do now, impossible to
# reconstruct later. Segment comes from the prefix only — everything after the
# first `-` is yours to name, so the version costs nothing.
#
#   qr-  -> pro       the founder card, consumer
#   ref- -> direct    a real person sent them, but we do not know why
#
# Both land on #quote rather than the top of the page. A card is handed over in
# person, so the recipient already had the pitch — what they need is the form.
# The tradeoff is that the segment hero never gets seen; drop the fragment to
# land them on it instead. Attribution is recorded either way.
/q        /?src=qr-card-founder-01&utm_source=card&utm_medium=print&utm_campaign=founder#quote    302
/friend   /?src=ref-card-friend-01&utm_source=card&utm_medium=print&utm_campaign=referral#quote   302

# /book is the opt-in URL named in Twilio's A2P 10DLC campaign registration.
# A reviewer follows it by hand to confirm the consent checkbox is really there
# and really unchecked, so it has to land ON the booking form, not the homepage
# top. Untagged on purpose: this is a compliance URL, not a marketing one, and
# it must not pollute attribution with a src that no campaign ever printed.
/book     /#quote             302
